.TH WAVE-MIRROR 1 "" "MacWave" "MacWave Manual"

.SH NAME
wave-mirror \- Show the address each kind of data is fetched from, including the built-in defaults for anything not overridden by an environment variable.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wave mirror [flags]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Show the address each kind of data is fetched from, including the
built-in defaults for anything not overridden by an environment
variable.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print the configuration as JSON
.TP
.B \-\-yaml
Print the configuration as YAML
.TP
.B \-\-toml
Print the configuration as TOML
.TP
.B \-\-raw
Print ready-to-paste export lines
.TP
.B \-\-only\-set
With --raw: export only the sources you overrode, leaving the rest to
follow the built-in defaults
.TP
.B \-\-show\-password
Print passwords in full instead of six asterisks
.TP
.B \-\-hide\-user
Also mask the user name

.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
wave mirror
wave mirror --raw
wave mirror --json
wave mirror --show-password
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
wave(1)
